## Core principles
- Research -> analysis -> approved plan -> isolated workspace -> instructions -> implementation.
- English work, Chinese user reports. No deletion of any path lacking yihou. No unrequested commits.
- Docker for experiments. Keep authored files, logs, downloaded artifacts, tmp and caches in this workspace.
- Use iterative-debug-loop: numbered rounds with hypothesis, commands, evidence, outcomes, minimal next change. Differential comparison against reference mandatory; use three evidence sources for serious diagnoses.
- Leader owns deployment/benchmarks; expert8-research owns independent SGLang patch/tests. Do not delegate verification of leader work.
- Re-read mission every10min and at phase boundaries. Leader checks teammates every20min: first issue record only; intervene next check if unresolved.
- LSP and Serena for source navigation. Report unavailable capabilities honestly.

## Notable details
- CUDA graph compilation may take30min. Inspect live container logs/cache progress before declaring a hang.
- Pin corresponding RDMA rails per GPU, preserve PD rank affinity, verify GPU transfer bytes before bring-up.
- Reset only task-owned resources between retries; verify GPU memory returned to idle before relaunch.
- Never change MC_DISABLE_HIP_TRANSPORT into another spelling; never set MC_DISABLE_HIP=1 or MC_USE_HIP_IPC=0.
- Existing semantic smoke asserts Jupiter/tool correctness: do not use those assertions for synthetic model.
- Auto-sized KV allocation hides weight savings in total rocm-smi VRAM; measure weight/KV split and token capacity.
